BT /F1 9 Tf 50 216 Td (   violation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 203 Td (BR-03  |  Courses are ordered by enrolment descending, credits descending, and course code.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 190 Td (   Each is placed in the earliest feasible session, preferring a gap-compliant placement. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 177 Td (   bounded deterministic repair pass displaces only blocking assignments to recover) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 164 Td (   unscheduled courses; backlog courses remain restricted to their permitted final sessions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 151 Td (BR-04  |  Total enrolment in a session may not exceed 90% of available hall capacity. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 138 Td (   integer threshold is rounded down. Two- and three-hour exams cannot share a hall.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 125 Td (BR-05  |  Halls are considered largest first. Each holds at most two courses; courses must) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 112 Td (   be from different departments; courses with fewer than 10 students must share. Exactly 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 99 Td (   students may use a hall alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 86 Td (BR-06  |  Seats are row-major; students are sorted by register number within course queues) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 73 Td (   and placed in alternating columns to avoid adjacent same-course seats. Special-needs) Tj ET
