BT /F1 9 Tf 50 748 Td (   students require row 1 of a ground-floor hall; unseated students receive an explicit) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 735 Td (   status. Special-needs priority takes precedence over the general queue order.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 722 Td (BR-07  |  Each hall requires `ceil\(students / 30\)` invigilators, minimum one, plus one chief) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 709 Td (   per building/session. Hall invigilators cannot invigilate their own department's course.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 696 Td (   All staff are limited to two sessions/day and their weekly maximum; unavailable) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 683 Td (   dates/periods and special-needs extensions are respected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 670 Td (BR-08  |  Eligible invigilators are ordered by assigned load, department, then ID. A chief) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 657 Td (   is reserved before hall staffing and attached to a compatible hall in the building.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 50 644 Td (   Unavailable dates/periods are respected. Exhaustion produces an explicit `UNSTAFFED`) Tj ET
